WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.850
Every injury crash in Ohio ends up in a police report.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.350
Pick your counties on the map, or search one police agency statewide.

3
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.570
You choose the AI model and mode, and you see the cost per report before you start.

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.680
Then clear one quick CAPTCHA per search. That's the only manual step.

5
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:25.930
The scanner pulls the injury reports and reads every one. This run: twenty-six reports, about five cents.

6
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.460
Then your dashboard lights up. Every lead, by county and injury.

7
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.920
Hover any county to see its leads.

8
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.990
Click one, and the whole dashboard filters to it.

9
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.010
Every lead lands in one clean list, ready to export.

10
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.370
Looking for one crash? Search by city, date or report number.

11
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.760
Rather not run the software? We'll run it for you and deliver the leads up to twice a week.

12
00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.570
The Ohio Crash Report Analysis Tool. From Tevis Engineering.
